  "body": "Found in the review of PR 1485. `sed_in_place` in `web/build-app-wasm.sh` (about line 58) runs sed and the move in an `&&` list, and bash ignores `set -e` inside such a list, so a failing sed does not stop the script. The two earlier edits are re-checked by `grep` afterwards, but the `sed_in_place '1d'` call is not: a failure there shows up only later, as a compile error.\n\nWanted: the helper returns non-zero when sed or the move fails (`|| return 1`), and every caller stops on that.\n\nDone means: a failing sed in `sed_in_place` ends the script with a message naming the file; `bash -n` passes; behaviour on a successful run is unchanged.\n",
